{"id":"mahabharata-1-055","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":55,"title":"पञ्चपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 55 · Vaishampayana tells the story in brief","summary":{"en":"Vaishampayana bows to his teacher and first tells the epic in outline: the Pandavas' upbringing, Duryodhana's plots, the house of lac, the winning of Draupadi, the dice game, the exile, and the war that ended in their victory.","kn":"ಗುರುವಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸಿ ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನನು ಮೊದಲು ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಸಂಕ್ಷೇಪವಾಗಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಪಾಂಡವರ ಬಾಲ್ಯ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಕುತಂತ್ರಗಳು, ಅರಗಿನ ಮನೆ, ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯ ಪ್ರಾಪ್ತಿ, ಜೂಜು, ವನವಾಸ ಮತ್ತು ಅವರ ವಿಜಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಮುಗಿದ ಯುದ್ಧ.","hi":"गुरु को प्रणाम कर वैशम्पायन पहले संक्षेप में कथा कहते हैं: पाण्डवों का पालन-पोषण, दुर्योधन के षड्यन्त्र, लाक्षागृह, द्रौपदी की प्राप्ति, द्यूत, वनवास और उनकी विजय में समाप्त हुआ युद्ध।","te":"గురువుకు నమస్కరించి వైశంపాయనుడు మొదట కథను సంక్షిప్తంగా చెబుతాడు: పాండవుల పెంపకం, దుర్యోధనుని కుట్రలు, లక్కఇల్లు, ద్రౌపదీ లాభం, జూదం, వనవాసం, వారి విజయంతో ముగిసిన యుద్ధం.","ta":"குருவை வணங்கி வைஶம்பாயனர் முதலில் கதையைச் சுருக்கமாகச் சொல்கிறார்: பாண்டவர்களின் வளர்ப்பு, துரியோதனனின் சூழ்ச்சிகள், அரக்கு மாளிகை, திரௌபதியை அடைதல், சூது, வனவாசம், அவர்களின் வெற்றியில் முடிந்த போர்.","ml":"ഗുരുവിനെ വണങ്ങി വൈശമ്പായനൻ ആദ്യം ഇതിഹാസത്തിന്റെ രൂപരേഖ പറയുന്നു: പാണ്ഡവരുടെ വളർച്ച, ദുര്യോധനന്റെ കുതന്ത്രങ്ങൾ, അരക്കില്ലം, ദ്രൗപദിയുടെ സ്വയംവരം, ചൂതുകളി, വനവാസം, ഒടുവിൽ അവരുടെ വിജയത്തിൽ അവസാനിക്കുന്ന യുദ്ധം."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.55; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अंशावतरणपर्व","titleEn":"Amshavatarana Parva (Partial incarnations)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गुरवे प्राङ्नमस्कृत्य मनोबुद्धिसमाधिभिः ।\nसंपूज्य च द्विजान्सर्वांस्तथान्यान्विदुषो जनान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"First bowing to my teacher with mind, intellect and concentration, and honoring all the brahmins and other learned people,"}},{"n":2,"text":"महर्षेः सर्वलोकेषु विश्रुतस्यास्य धीमतः ।\nप्रवक्ष्यामि मतं कृत्स्नं व्यासस्यामिततेजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell in full the thought of this great sage, wise and of boundless power, Vyasa, famed in all the worlds."}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रोतुं पात्रं च राजंस्त्वं प्राप्येमां भारतीं कथाम् ।\nगुरोर्वक्तुं परिस्पन्दो मुदा प्रोत्साहतीव माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are a fit hearer, king, of this tale of the Bharatas; my teacher's command, with joy, seems to urge me on to tell it."}},{"n":4,"text":"शृणु राजन्यथा भेदः कुरुपाण्डवयोरभूत् ।\nराज्यार्थे द्यूतसंभूतो वनवासस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, king, to how the quarrel arose between the Kurus and the Pandavas, how the exile in the forest came from the dice game over the kingdom."}},{"n":5,"text":"यथा च युद्धमभवत्पृथिवीक्षयकारकम् ।\nतत्तेऽहं संप्रवक्ष्यामि पृच्छते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how the war came that destroyed the earth: I will tell you all that, bull of the Bharatas, since you ask."}},{"n":6,"text":"मृते पितरि ते वीरा वनादेत्य स्वमन्दिरम् ।\nनचिरादिव विद्वांसो वेदे धनुषि चाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When their father died, those heroes came from the forest to their own house, and before long became learned in the Veda and in archery."}},{"n":7,"text":"तांस्तथा रूपवीर्यौजःसंपन्नान्पौरसंमतान् ।\nनामृष्यन्कुरवो दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवाञ्श्रीयशोभृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus could not bear to see the Pandavas, endowed with beauty, valor and vigor, esteemed by the townsfolk, and wearing glory and fame."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनः क्रूरः कर्णश्च सहसौबलः ।\nतेषां निग्रहनिर्वासान्विविधांस्ते समाचरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then cruel Duryodhana, with Karna and Shakuni, son of Subala, devised various ways to restrain and banish them."}},{"n":9,"text":"ददावथ विषं पापो भीमाय धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nजरयामास तद्वीरः सहान्नेन वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sinful son of Dhritarashtra gave poison to Bhima; the hero Vrikodara digested it along with the food."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रमाणकोट्यां संसुप्तं पुनर्बद्ध्वा वृकोदरम् ।\nतोयेषु भीमं गङ्गायाः प्रक्षिप्य पुरमाव्रजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhima lay asleep at Pramanakoti, Duryodhana bound him, threw him into the waters of the Ganga, and went back to the city."}},{"n":11,"text":"यदा प्रबुद्धः कौन्तेयस्तदा संछिद्य बन्धनम् ।\nउदतिष्ठन्महाराज भीमसेनो गतव्यथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Kunti's son woke, Bhimasena, great king, broke his bonds and rose up, unharmed."}},{"n":12,"text":"आशीविषैः कृष्णसर्पैः सुप्तं चैनमदंशयत् ।\nसर्वेष्वेवाङ्गदेशेषु न ममार च शत्रुहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he slept, they had black venomous snakes bite him on every part of his body, yet that slayer of foes did not die."}},{"n":13,"text":"तेषां तु विप्रकारेषु तेषु तेषु महामतिः ।\nमोक्षणे प्रतिघाते च विदुरोऽवहितोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In each of these wrongs against them, the very wise Vidura was watchful in freeing them and in countering the plots."}},{"n":14,"text":"स्वर्गस्थो जीवलोकस्य यथा शक्रः सुखावहः ।\nपाण्डवानां तथा नित्यं विदुरोऽपि सुखावहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Indra, dwelling in heaven, brings happiness to the world of the living, so Vidura always brought happiness to the Pandavas."}},{"n":15,"text":"यदा तु विविधोपायैः संवृतैर्विवृतैरपि ।\nनाशक्नोद्विनिहन्तुं तान्दैवभाव्यर्थरक्षितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When with various devices, hidden and open, he could not kill them, for they were protected by what fate had ordained,"}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः संमन्त्र्य सचिवैर्वृषदुःशासनादिभिः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रमनुज्ञाप्य जातुषं गृहमादिशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"he consulted his counselors, Karna, Duhshasana and others, obtained Dhritarashtra's leave, and ordered a house of lac to be built."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत्र तान्वासयामास पाण्डवानमितौजसः ।\nअदाहयच्च विस्रब्धान्पावकेन पुनस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he made the Pandavas of boundless power live, and then, when they felt secure, had it set on fire."}},{"n":18,"text":"विदुरस्यैव वचनात्खनित्री विहिता ततः ।\nमोक्षयामास योगेन ते मुक्ताः प्राद्रवन्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Vidura's word a tunnel had been made; by that device he freed them, and once free they fled in fear."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततो महावने घोरे हिडिम्बं नाम राक्षसम् ।\nभीमसेनोऽवधीत्क्रुद्धो भुवि भीमपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in a great terrible forest the fierce Bhimasena, of fearful valor, angrily killed a rakshasa named Hidimba on the ground."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथ संधाय ते वीरा एकचक्रां व्रजंस्तदा ।\nब्रह्मरूपधरा भूत्वा मात्रा सह परंतपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those heroes, tormentors of foes, taking the form of brahmins, went with their mother to Ekachakra."}},{"n":21,"text":"तत्र ते ब्राह्मणार्थाय बकं हत्वा महाबलम् ।\nब्राह्मणैः सहिता जग्मुः पाञ्चालानां पुरं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, for the sake of a brahmin family, they killed the very strong Baka, and then went with brahmins to the city of the Panchalas."}},{"n":22,"text":"ते तत्र द्रौपदीं लब्ध्वा परिसंवत्सरोषिताः ।\nविदिता हास्तिनपुरं प्रत्याजग्मुररिंदमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There they won Draupadi, lived a year, and when they became known, those subduers of enemies returned to Hastinapura."}},{"n":23,"text":"त उक्ता धृतराष्ट्रेण राज्ञा शांतनवेन च ।\nभ्रातृभिर्विग्रहस्तात कथं वो न भवेदिति ।\nअस्माभिः खाण्डवप्रस्थे युष्मद्वासोऽनुचिन्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Dhritarashtra and Bhishma, son of Shantanu, told them: \"Child, so that no quarrel may arise among you brothers, we have considered that you should live at Khandavaprastha.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्माज्जनपदोपेतं सुविभक्तमहापथम् ।\nवासाय खाण्डवप्रस्थं व्रजध्वं गतमन्यवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So go, free of anger, to live at Khandavaprastha, a place with a populated country and well-laid great roads.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"तयोस्ते वचनाज्जग्मुः सह सर्वैः सुहृज्जनैः ।\nनगरं खाण्डवप्रस्थं रत्नान्यादाय सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At their word they went, with all their friends, to the city of Khandavaprastha, taking jewels of every kind."}},{"n":26,"text":"तत्र ते न्यवसन्राजन्संवत्सरगणान्बहून् ।\nवशे शस्त्रप्रतापेन कुर्वन्तोऽन्यान्महीक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There they lived, king, for many years, bringing other kings under their sway by the power of their weapons."}},{"n":27,"text":"एवं धर्मप्रधानास्ते सत्यव्रतपरायणाः ।\nअप्रमत्तोत्थिताः क्षान्ताः प्रतपन्तोऽहितांस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, putting dharma first and devoted to their vow of truth, watchful, active and forbearing, they then scorched their enemies."}},{"n":28,"text":"अजयद्भीमसेनस्तु दिशं प्राचीं महाबलः ।\nउदीचीमर्जुनो वीरः प्रतीचीं नकुलस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Bhimasena conquered the east, the hero Arjuna the north, Nakula the west,"}},{"n":29,"text":"दक्षिणां सहदेवस्तु विजिग्ये परवीरहा ।\nएवं चक्रुरिमां सर्वे वशे कृत्स्नां वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and Sahadeva, slayer of enemy heroes, conquered the south. Thus they all brought the whole earth under their rule."}},{"n":30,"text":"पञ्चभिः सूर्यसंकाशैः सूर्येण च विराजता ।\nषट्सूर्येवाबभौ पृथ्वी पाण्डवैः सत्यविक्रमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the five of them like suns, and the shining one more, the earth seemed to have six suns, thanks to the Pandavas of true valor."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततो निमित्ते कस्मिंश्चिद्धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nवनं प्रस्थापयामास भ्रातरं वै धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, for some reason, Yudhishthira, the king of dharma, sent his brother Dhananjaya to the forest."}},{"n":32,"text":"स वै संवत्सरं पूर्णं मासं चैकं वनेऽवसत् ।\nततोऽगच्छद्धृषीकेशं द्वारवत्यां कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"He lived there a full year and a month, and then at one time went to Hrishikesha at Dvaravati."}},{"n":33,"text":"लब्धवांस्तत्र बीभत्सुर्भार्यां राजीवलोचनाम् ।\nअनुजां वासुदेवस्य सुभद्रां भद्रभाषिणीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Bibhatsu won as his wife the lotus-eyed Subhadra of gentle speech, younger sister of Vasudeva."}},{"n":34,"text":"सा शचीव महेन्द्रेण श्रीः कृष्णेनेव संगता ।\nसुभद्रा युयुजे प्रीता पाण्डवेनार्जुनेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Shachi joins Mahendra and Shri joins Krishna, so Subhadra was happily united with the Pandava Arjuna."}},{"n":35,"text":"अतर्पयच्च कौन्तेयः खाण्डवे हव्यवाहनम् ।\nबीभत्सुर्वासुदेवेन सहितो नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Kunti's son, Bibhatsu, together with Vasudeva, satisfied the fire god at Khandava, best of kings."}},{"n":36,"text":"नातिभारो हि पार्थस्य केशवेनाभवत्सह ।\nव्यवसायसहायस्य विष्णोः शत्रुवधेष्विव ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was no great burden to Partha when he had Keshava with him, as for Vishnu, with his resolve as helper, in the killing of foes."}},{"n":37,"text":"पार्थायाग्निर्ददौ चापि गाण्डीवं धनुरुत्तमम् ।\nइषुधी चाक्षयैर्बाणै रथं च कपिलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fire god also gave Partha the finest bow Gandiva, two quivers with inexhaustible arrows, and a chariot with an ape on its banner."}},{"n":38,"text":"मोक्षयामास बीभत्सुर्मयं तत्र महासुरम् ।\nस चकार सभां दिव्यां सर्वरत्नसमाचिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Bibhatsu freed the great asura Maya, who built a divine assembly hall studded with every kind of jewel."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्यां दुर्योधनो मन्दो लोभं चक्रे सुदुर्मतिः ।\nततोऽक्षैर्वञ्चयित्वा च सौबलेन युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that hall dull-witted, wicked Duryodhana conceived greed; then Shakuni, son of Subala, cheated Yudhishthira at dice."}},{"n":40,"text":"वनं प्रस्थापयामास सप्त वर्षाणि पञ्च च ।\nअज्ञातमेकं राष्ट्रे च तथा वर्षं त्रयोदशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He sent him to the forest for twelve years, and a thirteenth year, to be lived unknown within the kingdom."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततश्चतुर्दशे वर्षे याचमानाः स्वकं वसु ।\nनालभन्त महाराज ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in the fourteenth year, when they asked for their own wealth, they did not get it, great king, and so war broke out."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततस्ते सर्वमुत्साद्य हत्वा दुर्योधनं नृपम् ।\nराज्यं विद्रुतभूयिष्ठं प्रत्यपद्यन्त पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having destroyed everyone and killed King Duryodhana, the Pandavas regained a kingdom mostly in ruins."}},{"n":43,"text":"एवमेतत्पुरावृत्तं तेषामक्लिष्टकर्मणाम् ।\nभेदो राज्यविनाशश्च जयश्च जयतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"So this is what happened in the past to those of untroubled deeds: the quarrel, the ruin of the kingdom, and victory, best of the victorious."}}]}]}